      "name": "Question 4",
      "problem": "${(6\\cdot 8)}^{3}\\cdot {6}^{5}=$",
      "worked_solution": "First, we rewrite the second factor using the power of product rule:\n\n$$\n{(6\\cdot 8)}^{3}\\cdot {6}^{5}={6}^{3}\\cdot {8}^{3}\\cdot {6}^{5}\n$$\n\nFinally, we apply the product rule for exponents, and simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{6}^{3}\\cdot {8}^{3}\\cdot {6}^{5} & ={6}^{3}\\cdot {6}^{5}\\cdot {8}^{3} \\\\  & ={6}^{3+5}\\cdot {8}^{3} \\\\  & ={6}^{8}\\cdot {8}^{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
